think Opened cold as the directive asks: sh tools/fixtures/standing_equipment_run.sh read 42 guards, 39 green, 3 red -- geode_libraries, readme_metrics, tracked_link. The previous lap's own cold open had read 41 of 41 green, so the three reds arrived between those two runs and the tree in between was the previous lap's staged work.
think Standfast. The line stops at a red, so the image round the last recommend named waits behind these three. Ran each guard alone to find its root rather than reasoning about it.
think tracked_link named the file: construction/ITINERARY.md cites ../active-designing/20260824-080208_the-roster-that-decides-what-gets-measured.md, and git status read that path as ?? -- written, cited from a living card, never added. The guard's founding case is a reference that resolves here and breaks in a clone; this is the same fault from a direction it had not seen, a file never added rather than a symlink gone stale.
think readme_metrics: the README block read 1669 witnesses, a fresh render read 1670. geode_libraries: the generated library index read one witness short in five rooms at once -- constel 33 against 34, crypto 114 against 115, glow 104 against 105, image 246 against 247, lotus 239 against 240. One cause for both: the round added tools/l/living_docs_roster_witness.rish and every page that counts witnesses moved.
think Before writing a prevention I asked whether one already stood, since REDS %151 and %152 are this same class. tools/hooks/pre-commit exists, is mode 100755, core.hooksPath names tools/hooks, and tools/g/generated_page_freshness_witness.rish proves on throwaway repositories that it regenerates BOTH pages and stages them into the commit that added the witness. So the machinery is whole and fires at git commit.
think That settles the root and it is one sentence: the lap staged eleven paths and committed none, so the hook never ran. The pre-commit hook would have repaired two of the three automatically, and git add -A would have carried the third. No new guard is wanted here, and writing one would be building a second copy of what already stands.
think Repaired in order: git add -A for the essay, then readme_metrics.rish write, then geode_libraries.rish write, then all three guards re-run GREEN on metal. Shipped the whole staged round as one signed commit 7b987463b7, whose own pre-commit hook found nothing left to refresh -- which is the hook agreeing with the hand.
obs The council rota row this lap was row 3365 mod 5 = 0, Aether and Jupiter, why the work exists: follow-our-compass, the-lindy-effect-and-the-long-return, the-grain-and-the-crossing. The Lindy piece names a README as the most Lindy-exposed artifact a project owns, read first and cited most, and that is exactly the queue this lap inherits -- image/README.md at 400,042 bytes. The compass says brief and green witnesses win, which is why the roster's reading outranked the recommend line, and the reds were taken first.
obs The honest finding is that the prevention was already whole and the lap stopped one step short of reaching it. That is a different shape of red from the last four, which each found a roster short of its directory. Here nothing was missing; a step was skipped, and every guard that exists to catch it caught it -- one lap later than it could have, because they run at commit and at the roster's hot pass.
obs No guard can enforce that a lap commits, since such a guard would have to run after the lap ends. Naming that limit in the ledger and the operator card is better than shipping a check that looks like coverage and is not.
obs Measured beside it, because the reason a directive gets skipped is usually its price: the three census guards together run in 67 seconds, and the full roster of 42 ran in 454 seconds warm on this pier. Roughly a seventh of the cost catches exactly this class, which is worth knowing on a lap that is deciding whether to run the hot pass.
obs Booking %188 carried construction/REDS.md past its 24,576-byte bound, so row %184 folded to construction/archive/. Its three ../tools/ links were deepened to ../../tools/ and the header's own ../REDS.md left as the destination writes it -- %186's rule applied rather than rediscovered.
